  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MERALCO Power Distribution Modernization Pilot Project, through Nexant, Inc.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This feasibility study grant would support Manila Electric Company ( MERALCO) to develop the technical scope and implementation plan for a power distribution modernization pilot project that will address its distribution issues and improve customer services. The pilot would install 10,000 smart meters in MERALCOs metro Manila franchise, and is expected to help optimize transmission and distribution services for system-wide implementation of smart grid technologies, and reduce non-payment by customers and distribution losses. This $6,750 contract modification funds the third party invoice and deliverable consultant to assist USTDA with reviewing an additional deliverable and corresponding invoice associated with the Burma Energy Transaction Advisory Services Technical Assistance (USTDA Activity No. 2015-31017A).</narrative>
  </description>
